Science Against Authoritarianism (Pharos) — AUTHORS
===================================================

Pharos is a project for the public, built for the good of humanity and
the environment. It carries no personal credit: it is offered free of
charge, and the people who build it seek no personal recognition. In
copyright and license notices, the contributors are credited
collectively as "The Pharos contributors".

Contributions
-------------

All original contributions in this repository — the research
synthesis, the framing of the four-lens analysis, the design of the
proposed initiative, the methodology, the tools, and the original prose
in all .md files — are by The Pharos contributors.

Third-party datasets (the World Bank Worldwide Governance Indicators,
V-Dem, Freedom House, and those the design proposes, such as ACLED,
UCDP and GDELT), software dependencies, and cited peer-reviewed
literature carry their own authorship and licensing and are not part
of this AUTHORS list.

AI-assisted development
-----------------------

The research synthesis and the tools were developed with AI assistance
(Claude by Anthropic, and other AI coding assistants) under human
direction. All retained claims, citations, and the public text of the
deliverables are checked by a human contributor against cited,
measured sources. AI assistants are not authors and hold no copyright
in this work.

Future contributors
-------------------

Contributions from third parties are accepted under the licenses
mapped in LICENSE and REUSE.toml and the process in CONTRIBUTING.md. Contributors are credited collectively
as "The Pharos contributors"; anyone who wishes to be named
individually may add themselves to this file with their first merged
contribution.

-- end AUTHORS --
